---
import { Icon } from 'astro-icon/components';
---

<div class="card-purple">
  <div class="flex items-start gap-4 mb-6">
    <div class="flex-shrink-0 hidden lg:flex">
      <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-full bg-primary-600/10 flex items-center justify-center">
        <Icon name="line-md:star-filled" class="text-primary-600 text-2xl" />
      </div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-2 text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Platform Infrastructure at Scale</h3>
      <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-400">
        This wasn't a feature—it was <strong>foundational infrastructure</strong> that automated compliance and enabled every engineer to ship high-quality work without bottlenecking expert teams. Platform engineering lessons from making standards scalable.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
        <Icon name="line-md:confirm-circle" class="text-primary-600 flex-shrink-0 text-xl mt-1" />
        <div>
          <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1 dark:text-white">Automated Compliance at Scale</h4>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
            When standards are complex and constantly evolving, automation becomes critical. The system validates adherence to standards automatically—WCAG accessibility, design tokens, component patterns—catching issues before they reach production.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
        <Icon name="line-md:confirm-circle" class="text-primary-600 flex-shrink-0 text-xl mt-1" />
        <div>
          <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1 dark:text-white">Trust Through Transparency</h4>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
            Developers won't trust "AI magic"—they need to understand the reasoning. Every recommendation includes citations to source documentation and clear explanations, building confidence through transparency rather than black-box automation.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
        <Icon name="line-md:confirm-circle" class="text-primary-600 flex-shrink-0 text-xl mt-1" />
        <div>
          <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1 dark:text-white">Developer-First Experience</h4>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
            Platform tools only succeed if they integrate into existing workflows. VS Code, GitHub, and CLI integrations meet developers where they already work, avoiding context switches and dashboard friction that kill adoption.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-4">
      <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
        <Icon name="line-md:confirm-circle" class="text-primary-600 flex-shrink-0 text-xl mt-1" />
        <div>
          <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1 dark:text-white">Continuous Monitoring & Remediation</h4>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
            Real-time validation during development prevents drift and catches issues early. By surfacing problems as developers write code, the system reduces expensive fixes later while maintaining compliance continuously rather than through periodic audits.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
        <Icon name="line-md:confirm-circle" class="text-primary-600 flex-shrink-0 text-xl mt-1" />
        <div>
          <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1 dark:text-white">Platform Infrastructure Thinking</h4>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
            Built as <strong>foundational infrastructure that enables other engineers</strong>, not a point solution. The MCP protocol powers multiple integrations (IDE, CI/CD, dashboards) and is designed for extensibility—solving today's problems while architecting for the 5-year horizon.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
        <Icon name="line-md:confirm-circle" class="text-primary-600 flex-shrink-0 text-xl mt-1" />
        <div>
          <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1 dark:text-white">Measurable Business Impact</h4>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
            Platform investments require business justification. Measured and tracked concrete outcomes: $2.3M annual savings, 94% compliance rates, 52% efficiency gains. ROI data secured continued funding and proved the value of infrastructure work.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-8 pt-6 border-t border-primary-600/20 dark:border-primary-400/20">
    <div class="bg-white/50 rounded-lg p-4 md:p-6 dark:bg-black/40">
      <h4 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2 flex items-center gap-2 dark:text-white">
        <Icon name="line-md:lightbulb-twotone" class="text-primary-600 text-xl flex-shrink-0 dark:text-primary-400" />
        Core Lesson: Making Standards Scalable
      </h4>
      <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed dark:text-gray-400">
        The fundamental challenge in platform engineering: <strong>How do you ensure thousands of people follow complex standards without creating bottlenecks or burning out expert teams?</strong> The solution is intelligent automation that educates, validates, and guides—making every engineer more capable while freeing experts to focus on strategic initiatives rather than repetitive support.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
